<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lower Franconia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Unterfranken</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a> is an administrative region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, in the north-west of the state along the Main river, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wurzburg">Würzburg</a> as its seat. Largely formed from the lands of the former prince-bishopric of Würzburg and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aschaffenburg">Aschaffenburg</a> area, it came under Bavaria in 1814 and is known for its Franconian wine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lower-franconia.jpg" alt="Lower Franconia" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zebra848 (gif) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Lower_Franconia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
